{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And he was in Chezib.</b> The reason he named him Shelah after the sense of אַל תַּשְׁלֶה — \"do not delay\" (II Kings 4:28) — is that it is an unfitting name, because Judah was then in Chezib, and her hope was disappointed [נִכְזְבָה] from seeing her husband's face at the time she gave birth. For had he been there, he would not have consented to the giving of an unfitting name."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:33:45.224095213Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}